mRegularity -- compute Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        mRegularity I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous *note Ideal:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CM (missing documentation) => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, a parameter that should be
        set to *note true: (Macaulay2Doc)true, if the ideal is known to be
        Cohen-Macaulay
      * MonCurve (missing documentation) => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false,  parameter that should be
        set to true if I is the ideal of a monomial curve
      * Verbose (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of the given ideal, if it is
        homogeneous, and -1 otherwise

